<!--
  Right bud — APP COPY, high-resolution trace. Mirror of ic_bud_left_hq.xml.

  Produced by mirroring the left bud about x = 24 (`scaleX="-1"` with a translate
  of 2 * 24 = 48) rather than tracing the right bud separately. That is the right
  call here for two reasons:
    1. The two buds are the same object rotated, so a mirror is geometrically
       correct, and it guarantees the pair is perfectly symmetrical — which
       matters in the battery panel, where the two icons sit side by side and any
       asymmetry is obvious.
    2. It means only ONE path needs to be kept in sync if the artwork is ever
       retraced, instead of two.

  The mirror is applied INSIDE the normalising group, so the ink-centring
  correction from ic_bud_left_hq.xml still applies afterwards (mirror uses the
  viewport centre, which the correction also targets, so the composition of the
  two is stable).
-->
